ask(c,'Using first-quadrant trigonometric values and symmetry, what are sin150° and cos150°?', ['1/2 and −√3/2','−1/2 and √3/2','1/2 and √3/2','−√3/2 and1/2'], ['150° is in quadrantII with reference30°; sine positive, cosine negative.','These are the opposite signs.','Cosine must be negative in quadrantII.','This swaps values and signs.'],kind='numerical',steps=['150°=180°−30°.','sin(180°−a)=sin a;cos(180°−a)=−cos a.','Use sin30°=1/2,cos30°=√3/2.'],assumptions=['Angles in degrees; this is a generated illustration of the slide’s quarter-table symmetry.'])
